{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:7e6e6092c6905826","name":"Devourer","source":{"id":"source:reference-7e6e6092c6905826","title":"Devourer","revision":20392,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T23:45:51Z","sha256":"4ae63b7b3d667b2e104810cd43e23384f4e0174187cef716e0208ac3c8339b3f","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20392","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Devourer&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-7e6e6092c6905826","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["After the destruction of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Freedon Nadd"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Freedon_Nadd","referenceId":"reference:42a86011fff6acc7"},", Jedi Master ",{"tag":"a","children":["Arca Jeth"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Arca_Jeth","referenceId":"reference:18484a7f7c5135d1"}," is faced with a problem. He knows that any location where Nadd's remains are interred will be twisted by ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"},", but hiding the remains in an isolated place meant that Nadd could someday be rediscovered and reborn. Luckily, Araca finds a solution in one of the moons of the Onderon System. Known as the beast moon or the demon moon, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dxun"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dxun","referenceId":"reference:fe72b3042330089a"}," is a hostile place that deters trespassers, yet is closely monitored by ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"}," energies pouring out of Freedon Nadd's tomb took one of Dxun's deadliest predators and made it even more dangerous, giving rise to the Devourer, or what Jedi refer to as the Dxun Tomb Beast. A jagged horn juts from just below the creature's lower jaw, and the beast uses this horn to impale prey. It often hunts the cliffs near the tomb, jumping down upon unsuspecting trespassers and spiking them with this horn. The beast then uses its claws and teeth to tear flesh while toxic bacteria infect the wound.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Devourer Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Devourers are fiercely territorial and remarkably cunning. They defend their nests to the death and mate for life. Parents force their young out into the world soon after the young beasts have made their first kill. Attempts to breed Devourers offworld have proven unsuccessful. The creatures thrive in the Dark Side energies of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dxun"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dxun","referenceId":"reference:fe72b3042330089a"},". Yet many unsavory offworlders continue to capture these beasts, eager for a deadly pet or status symbol. Much as a blue milk run is seen as an easy job with many benefits and few dangers, a Dxun egg run is just the opposite. In fact, if a smuggler is sent on a Dxun egg run, chances are the time to pay back their loan has run out.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Devourer Statistics (CL 6)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Large Subterranean ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 7\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +4; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darkvision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darkvision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e3